# ============ What `vercel deploy` must never upload ============
# The Vercel CLI reads THIS file and not .gitignore: without it, a CLI deploy
# uploads the whole working tree — captures/ and fixtures/private/ included,
# which are raw palm frames and a recording of the user's face and hand. This
# product's promise is that a palm image never leaves the device; the deploy
# path must not be the thing that breaks it.
#
# Rule (D1.2): every line of .gitignore is repeated here verbatim
# (test/deploy-gate fails otherwise), so a CLI deploy uploads what a git deploy
# would. Anything else a deploy must never carry is added below the mirror.
# The D1.5 job deploys a `git archive` export, which never holds an ignored
# file in the first place; this file is the guard for a deploy run by hand.

# ---- mirror of .gitignore ----
node_modules
.next
out
.env*
!.env.example
diff.txt
*.log
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
lib/generated/
public/mediapipe/
public/ort/
captures/
scan-sessions/
*.session.zip
diff*.txt
test/eval/out/
fixtures/private/
fixtures/golden/**/raw/
fixtures/golden/**/snapshots/
.cache/
next-env.d.ts
.vercel
docs/reference/scan-video-*
docs/reference/phone-chamber-*

# ---- D1.5: never in a deploy, git-ignored or not ----
# every fixture (the eval sets are large and some are private), every
# reference image (the user's own stills), any video, and the build cache
fixtures/
docs/reference/
*.mp4
*.webm
.next/cache
